   "source": [
    "# Infrastructure Change Risk Agent\n",
    "\n",
    "## Persistent Memory Multi-Agent System\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements a **multi-agent pipeline** for assessing infrastructure change risks.\n",
    "Every change request, planner output, risk assessment, rollout strategy, incident, and final\n",
    "recommendation is stored and reused across sessions.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "User Change Request\n",
    "        |\n",
    "        v\n",
    "Memory Agent          (load previous incidents, changes, outputs)\n",
    "        |\n",
    "        v\n",
    "Planner Agent         (generate execution plan)\n",
    "        |\n",
    "        v\n",
    "Incident Retrieval    (FAISS vector search)\n",
    "        |\n",
    "        v\n",
    "Risk Agent            (assess risk level)\n",
    "        |\n",
    "        v\n",
    "Solution Agent        (generate mitigations)\n",
    "        |\n",
    "        v\n",
    "Rollout Agent         (design rollout strategy)\n",
    "        |\n",
    "        v\n",
    "Refiner Agent         (combine all outputs into executive report)\n",
    "        |\n",
    "        v\n",
    "Final Report + Memory Storage (JSON + FAISS)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Agents Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "| Agent | Role |\n",
    "|-------|------|\n",
    "| **Memory Agent** | Retrieves similar past changes, failures, and lessons |\n",
    "| **Planner Agent** | Generates step-by-step execution plan |\n",
    "| **Retrieval Agent** | Finds related incidents via FAISS vector search |\n",
    "| **Risk Agent** | Scores risk and identifies potential failures |\n",
    "| **Solution Agent** | Proposes preventive actions, testing, monitoring |\n",
    "| **Rollout Agent** | Designs canary/staged deployment strategy |\n",
    "| **Refiner Agent** | Produces a single executive-level report |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Cell 1: Install Dependencies\n",
    "\n",
    "Install the required packages:\n",
    "- `faiss-cpu` — Vector similarity search for incident retrieval\n",
    "- `sentence-transformers` — Embedding model to convert text into vectors\n",
    "- `openai` — OpenAI-compatible client (works with vLLM, Ollama, etc.)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install required packages (uncomment if needed)\n",
    "# !pip install faiss-cpu sentence-transformers openai"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Cell 2: Imports & Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "Set up all imports and configure the LLM endpoint.\n",
    "By default this points to a local vLLM server, but you can swap it\n",
    "for any OpenAI-compatible API (OpenAI, Ollama, etc.)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# -- Standard library --\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import faiss\n",
    "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n",
    "from openai import OpenAI\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- Suppress noisy warnings --\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- Configuration --\n",
    "# Point this to your LLM server (vLLM, Ollama, OpenAI, etc.)\n",
    "LLM_BASE_URL = os.getenv(\"LLM_BASE_URL\", \"http://localhost:8000/v1\")\n",
    "LLM_API_KEY  = os.getenv(\"LLM_API_KEY\", \"not-needed\")\n",
    "LLM_MODEL    = os.getenv(\"LLM_MODEL\", \"default\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# FAISS / embedding config\n",
    "EMBEDDING_MODEL = \"all-MiniLM-L6-v2\"  # Lightweight & fast sentence-transformer\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"LLM endpoint  : {LLM_BASE_URL}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Embedding model: {EMBEDDING_MODEL}\")\n",
    "print(\"Imports & configuration ready\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Cell 3: LLM Helper - `ask_llm()`\n",
    "\n",
    "A thin wrapper around the OpenAI-compatible chat completions API.\n",
    "All agents call this function to interact with the LLM."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a single reusable client pointing at the configured endpoint\n",
    "client = OpenAI(base_url=LLM_BASE_URL, api_key=LLM_API_KEY)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def ask_llm(prompt: str, temperature: float = 0.3) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Send a prompt to the LLM and return the assistant's reply.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Parameters\n",
    "    ----------\n",
    "    prompt : str\n",
    "        The full prompt text to send.\n",
    "    temperature : float\n",
    "        Controls randomness. Lower = more deterministic.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns\n",
    "    -------\n",
    "    str : The LLM's response text.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "        model=LLM_MODEL,\n",
    "        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n",
    "        temperature=temperature,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    return response.choices[0].message.content.strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"ask_llm() ready\")\n",
    "# Uncomment to test:\n",
    "# print(ask_llm(\"Say hello in one sentence.\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Cell 4: Generic Agent Helper - `ask_agent()`\n",
    "\n",
    "A role-based wrapper around `ask_llm()` that lets any agent\n",
    "act as a specialized persona. This is the foundation of the\n",
    "multi-agent architecture using a single LLM backend."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def ask_agent(role: str, task: str) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Invoke the LLM with a specific role and task.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Parameters\n",
    "    ----------\n",
    "    role : str\n",
    "        The persona the LLM should adopt (e.g. 'Risk Assessment Expert').\n",
    "    task : str\n",
    "        The specific task or question for the agent.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns\n",
    "    -------\n",
    "    str : The agent's response.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    prompt = f\"\"\"\n",
    "You are acting as:\n",
    "\n",
    "{role}\n",
    "\n",
    "Task:\n",
    "\n",
    "{task}\n",
    "\n",
    "Be concise and technical.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "    return ask_llm(prompt)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"ask_agent() ready\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
